# FunCommander

A retro game emulator and launcher for CHIP-8 games stored on an SD card
formatted with the FAT filesystem.

FunCommander mounts the board's SD card socket at `/sd` via `mm.fs.fat`,
scans and navigates directories, lists CHIP-8 ROM files (`.ch8`, `.c8`, `.rom`),
and launches them in an integrated, cycle-accurate CHIP-8 interpreter.

During gameplay, the 64x32 virtual screen is dynamically scaled onto the
display, with a full 16-key touch keypad for game controls, an on-screen
menu bar with pause/reset and launcher return, and sound timer tracking.
A built-in demo game ("Catch the Dot") is also provided so the emulator
can be evaluated even when an SD card is not inserted.
